# Director's Loan Balance (Biz Intel card)

## Formula (SSOT)

`calculateBusinessMetrics` closing liability (positive = company owes director):

\[
\text{Balance} = \text{Opening} + \text{Prior advances} + \text{Loan injections} + \text{Director-funded cash} - \text{Reimbursements} \pm \text{personal}
\]

## SELPIC FY display that looked wrong

| Line | Amount | Role |
|------|--------|------|
| Director-paid cash this period | $8,781.89 | + liability (setup costs) |
| Prior advances (auto-matched) | $8,781.89 | was + again (bug) |
| Loan injections | +$1,500 | bank Director Loan credit |
| Reimbursements paid | −$8,781.89 | bank repayment |
| **Shown balance** | **$10,281.89** | = $1,500 + **extra** $8,781.89 |

Economically after repay: should be **~$1,500** (remaining bank loan), not $10,281.89.

**Cause:** auto-match set prior = reimbursement total while the **same P&L window** already included those advances as Cash Expense `fundedByDirector`.

## Fix

`resolvePriorPeriodDirectorAdvances` when auto-match is on:

\[
\text{prior} = \max(0,\ \text{reimbursements} - \text{director-funded cash in window})
\]

Manual prior amount still wins when set.

Also: `calculateBusinessMetrics` must **add** `fundedByDirector` cash debits to DL (otherwise FY only moves on bank loan/reimburse lines). See `accounting-directors-loan-period-display.mdc`.

## Card lines (still correct as labels)

- **Director-paid company costs** — sum of funded cash in period (informational).
- **Prior advances** — residual lodgment plug after the fix (often $0 on Full statement / FY).
- **Loan injections / Reimbursements** — period movement detail.

## Do not

- Auto-match prior = full reimbursement total when funded cash already sits in the ledger window
- Treat $10,281.89 as correct FY closing when cash and repayments are both in-period
